{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/970200-newbie-question-human-mortals-as-playable-characters","id":970200,"title":"Newbie question: Human mortals as playable Characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T14:09:32-07:00","id":970200,"title":"Newbie question: Human mortals as playable Characters?","content":"I am quite new to Onyx Path RPGs and got intruiged by playing a common mortal human in Chronicles of Darkness. Now I got a glimpse of this new Storypath System which seems like a nice new step in evolution for the Storyteller System. I like &quot;playing a mortal&quot; part of Urban Fantasy, that's what got me into CoD/Hunter: the Vigil but as of now I seem to like the Storypath System more than the older Storyteller.<br /> So here to my questions:<br /> - Does Scion offer playing usual mortals as well or is it only about super heroes?<br /> - Is it possible to have the same Urban Fantasy feeling as in CoD/H:tV?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:14:16-07:00","id":970206,"title":"","content":"Scion: Origin is the 'corebook' for Scion 2e and is about playing as mortals. You won't be able to handle the threats that start showing up when things start going up to Hero/Demigod/God, but a major push in the new edition is allowing more urban fantasy adventures that aren't so epic in scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:05:03-07:00","id":972753,"title":"","content":"Is Origins focused on true mortals, or pre-Visitation Scions? Because a few comments from writers seem to indicate that pre-Visitation Scions are still somewhat mechanically different from pure mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:32:13-07:00","id":972774,"title":"","content":"Origins covers the basic mechanics along with urban fantasy playstyles, pre-Visitation Scions, and Antagonists suitable for that level of play (anything from human sorcerers to giants). There's also room for players to be one of the supernatural beings of the setting, so they can have the &quot;outside looking in&quot; perspective of the supernatural instead of the &quot;inside looking out&quot; one of more ordinary mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:07:34-07:00","id":972896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/970200-newbie-question-human-mortals-as-playable-characters?p=972753#post972753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Origins focused on true mortals, or pre-Visitation Scions? Because a few comments from writers seem to indicate that pre-Visitation Scions are still somewhat mechanically different from pure mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering the name, I'm going to have to say that Origins is about pre-Scions. More specifically, it's a prequel arc that leads up to your visitation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything specifically preventing you from playing a mortal, aside from the fact that you won't really be able to do anything of significant importance compared to Scions and Titanspawn. You would play a background character, there to lend support, but not do much else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-19-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}